{
  "title": "9: At-Tawbah التوبة",
  "data": "بَرَآءَةٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖۤ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ عَاهَدتُّمْ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ ؕ‏(1)\nBARAAA-ATUM MENAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI ELAL LAZEENA A’AHATTUM MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\n[This is] a [declaration of] repudiation by Allah and His Apostle [addressed] to the polytheists with whom you had made a treaty:\nفَسِيْحُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ اَرْبَعَةَ اَشْهُرٍ وَّاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّكُمْ غَيْرُ مُعْجِزِى اللّٰهِۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ مُخْزِى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(2)\nFA-SEEHOO FIL ARZE ARBA-A’TA ASH-HORINW WA’LAMOO ANNAKUM GHAYRO MO’JEZIL LAAHE, WA ANNAL LAAHA MUKHZIL KAAFEREEN.\nTravel [unmolested] in the land for four months, but know that you cannot frustrate Allah, and that Allah shall disgrace the faithless.\nوَاَذَانٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖۤ اِلَى النَّاسِ يَوْمَ الْحَجِّ الْاَكْبَرِ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ بَرِىْۤءٌ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ ۙ  وَ رَسُوْلُهٗ ؕ فَاِنْ تُبْتُمْ فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّكُمْ غَيْرُ مُعْجِزِى اللّٰهِ ؕ وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِعَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍۙ‏(3)\nWA AZAANUM MENAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI ELAN NAASE YAWMAL HAJJIL AKBARE ANNAL LAAHA BAREE-UM MENAL MUSHREKEENA, WA RASOOLOH, FA-IN TUBTUM FAHOWA KHAYRUL LAKUM, WA IN TAWALLAYTUM FA’LAMOO ANNAKUM GHAYRO MO’JEZIL LAAH, WA BASH-SHERIL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\n[This is] an announcement from Allah and His Apostle to all the people on the day of the greater Hajj: that Allah and His Apostle repudiate the polytheists: If you repent that is better for you; but if you turn your backs [on Allah], know that you cannot frustrate Allah, and inform the faithless of a painful punishment\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ عَاهَدتُّمْ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَنْقُصُوْكُمْ شَيْئًا وَّلَمْ يُظَاهِرُوْا عَلَيْكُمْ اَحَدًا فَاَتِمُّوْۤا اِلَيْهِمْ عَهْدَهُمْ اِلٰى مُدَّتِهِمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(4)\nILLAL LAZEENA A’AHATTUM MENAL MUSHREKEENA SUMMA LAM YANQOSOOKUM SHAY-ANW WA LAM YOZAAHEROO A’LAYKUM AHADAN FA-ATIMMOO ELAYHIM A’HDAHUM ELAA MUDDATEHIM, INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL MUTTAQEEN.\n(barring the polytheists with whom you have made a treaty, and who did not violate any [of its terms] with you, nor backed anyone against you. So fulfill the treaty with them until [the end of] its term. Indeed Allah loves the Godwary).\nفَاِذَا انْسَلَخَ الْاَشْهُرُ الْحُرُمُ فَاقْتُلُوا الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ حَيْثُ وَجَدْتُّمُوْهُمْ وَخُذُوْهُمْ وَاحْصُرُوْهُمْ وَاقْعُدُوْا لَهُمْ كُلَّ مَرْصَدٍ ۚ فَاِنْ تَابُوْا وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَ اٰتَوُا الزَّكٰوةَ فَخَلُّوْا سَبِيْلَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(5)\nFA-EZAN SALAKHAL ASH-HORUL HOROMO FAQTOLUL MUSHREKEENA HAYSO WAJATTOMOOHUM WA KHOZOOHUM WAH SOROOHUM WAQ O’DOO LAHUM KULLA MARSAD, FA-IN TAABOO WA AQAAMUS SALAATA WA AATAWUZ ZAKAATA FA-KHALLOO SABEELAHUM, INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nThen, when the sacred months have passed, kill the polytheists wherever you find them, capture them and besiege them, and lie in wait for them at every ambush. But if they repent, and maintain the prayer and give the zakat, then let them alone. Indeed Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nوَاِنْ اَحَدٌ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ اسْتَجَارَكَ فَاَجِرْهُ حَتّٰى يَسْمَعَ كَلَامَ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ اَبْلِغْهُ مَاْمَنَهٗ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(6)\nWA IN AHADUM MENAL MUSHREKEENAS TAJAARAKA FA-AJIRHO HATTAA YASMA-A’ KALAAMAL LAAHE SUMMA ABLIGH-HO MAAMANAH, ZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM QAWMUL LAA YA’LAMOON.\nIf any of the polytheists seeks asylum from you, grant him asylum until he hears the Word of Allah. Then convey him to his place of safety. That is because they are a people who do not know.\nكَيْفَ يَكُوْنُ لِلْمُشْرِكِيْنَ عَهْدٌ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَعِنْدَ رَسُوْلِهٖۤ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ عَاهَدتُّمْ عِنْدَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ۚ فَمَا اسْتَقَامُوْا لَكُمْ فَاسْتَقِيْمُوْا لَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(7)\nKAYFA YAKOONO LIL-MUSHREKEENA A’HDUN I’NDAL LAAHE WA I’NDA RASOOLEHI ILLAL LAZEENA A’AHATTUM I’NDAL MASJEDIL HARAAM, FAMAS TAQAAMOO LAKUM FASTAQEEMOO LAHUM, INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL MUTTAQEEN.\nHow shall the polytheists have any [valid] treaty with Allah and His Apostle?! (Barring those with whom you made a treaty at the Holy Mosque; so long as they are steadfast with you, be steadfast with them. Indeed Allah loves the Godwary.)\nكَيْفَ وَاِنْ يَّظْهَرُوْا عَلَيْكُمْ لَا يَرْقُبُوْا فِيْكُمْ اِلًّا وَّلَا ذِمَّةً ؕ يُرْضُوْنَكُمْ بِاَفْوَاهِهِمْ وَتَاْبٰى قُلُوْبُهُمْۚ وَاَكْثَرُهُمْ فٰسِقُوْنَۚ‏(8)\nKAYFA WA IN-Y YAZHAROO A’LAYKUM LAA YARQOBOO FEEKUM ILLANW WA LAA ZIMMAH, YURZOONAKUM BE-AFWAAHEHIM WA TAABAA QOLOOBOHUM, WA AKSAROHUM FAASEQOON.\nHow? For if, they get the better of you, they will observe toward you neither kinship nor covenant. They please you with their mouths while their hearts spurn you; and most of them are transgressors.\nاِشْتَرَوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا فَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ ؕ اِنَّهُمْ سَآءَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(9)\nISHTARAW BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE SAMANAN QALEELAN FA-SADDOO A’N SABEELEH, INNAHUM SAAA-A MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThey have sold the signs of Allah for a paltry gain, and have barred [the people] from His way. Evil indeed is what they have been doing.\nلَا يَرْقُبُوْنَ فِىْ مُؤْمِنٍ اِلًّا وَّلَا ذِمَّةً ؕ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُعْتَدُوْنَ‏(10)\nLAA YARQOBOONA FEE MOAMENIN ILLANW WA LAA ZIMMAH, WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MO’TADOON.\nThey observe toward a believer neither kinship nor covenant, and it is they who are the transgressors.\nفَاِنْ تَابُوْا وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَوُا الزَّكٰوةَ فَاِخْوَانُكُمْ فِى الدِّيْنِؕ وَنُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(11)\nFA-IN TAABOO WA AQAAMUS SALAATA WA AATAWUZ ZAKAATA FA-IKHWAANOKUM FID DEEN, WA NOFASSELUL AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’LAMOON.\nYet if they repent and maintain the prayer and give the zakat, then they are your brethren in faith. We elaborate the signs for a people who have knowledge.\nوَاِنْ نَّكَثُوْۤا اَيْمَانَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ عَهْدِهِمْ وَطَعَنُوْا فِىْ دِيْنِكُمْ فَقَاتِلُوْۤا اَئِمَّةَ الْكُفْرِۙ اِنَّهُمْ لَاۤ اَيْمَانَ لَهُمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَنْتَهُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA IN NAKASOO AYMAANAHUM MIM BA’DE A’HDEHIM WA TA-A’NOO FEE DEENEKUM FA-QAATELOO A-IMMATAL KUFRE, INNAHUM LAA AYMAANA LAHUM LA-A’LLAHUM YANTAHOON.\nBut if they break their pledges after their having made a treaty and revile your religion, then fight the leaders of unfaith—indeed, they have no [commitment to] pledges,—maybe they will desist.\nاَلَا تُقَاتِلُوْنَ قَوْمًا نَّكَثُوْۤا اَيْمَانَهُمْ وَهَمُّوْا بِاِخْرَاجِ الرَّسُوْلِ وَهُمْ بَدَءُوْكُمْ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ ؕ اَتَخْشَوْنَهُمْ ۚ فَاللّٰهُ اَحَقُّ اَنْ تَخْشَوْهُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(13)\nALAA TOQAATELOONA QAWMAN NAKASOO AYMAANAHUM WA HAMMOO BE-IKHRAAJIR RASOOLE WA HUM BADA-OOKUM AWWALA MARRAH, ATAKHSHAWNAHUM, FALLAAHO AHAQQO AN TAKHSHAWHO IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nWill you not make war on a people who broke their pledges and resolved to expel the Apostle, and opened [hostilities] against you initially? Do you fear them? But Allah is worthier of being feared by you, should you be faithful.\nقَاتِلُوْهُمْ يُعَذِّبْهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِاَيْدِيْكُمْ وَيُخْزِهِمْ وَيَنْصُرْكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَيَشْفِ صُدُوْرَ قَوْمٍ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَۙ‏(14)\nQAATELOOHUM YO-A’ZZIBHOMUL LAAHO BE-AYDEEKUM WA YUKHZEHIM WA YANSURKUM A’LAYHIM WA YASHFE SODOORA QAWMIM MOAMENEEN.\nMake war on them so that Allah may punish them by your hands and humiliate them, and help you against them, and heal the hearts of a faithful folk,\nوَيُذْهِبْ غَيْظَ قُلُوْبِهِمْ ؕ وَ يَتُوْبُ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(15)\nWA YUZHIB GHAYZA QOLOOBEHIM, WA YATOOBUL LAAHO A’LAA MAN-Y YASHAAA, WAL LAAHO A’LEEMUN HAKEEM.\nand remove rage from their hearts, and Allah turns clemently to whomever He wishes, and Allah is all-knowing, all-wise\nاَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ اَنْ تُتْرَكُوْا وَلَمَّا يَعْلَمِ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ جَاهَدُوْا مِنْكُمْ وَلَمْ يَتَّخِذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا رَسُوْلِهٖ وَلَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَلِيْجَةً ؕ وَاللّٰهُ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(16)\nAM HASIBTUM AN TUTRAKOO WA LAMMAA YA’LAMIL LAAHUL LAZEENA JAAHADOO MINKUM WA LAM YATTAKHEZOO MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA LAA RASOOLEHI WA LAL MOAMENEENA WALEEJAH, WAL LAAHO KHABEERUM BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nDo you suppose that you will be let off while Allah has not yet ascertained those of you who wage jihad and those who do not take anyone as [their] confidant besides Allah and His Apostle and the faithful? Allah is well aware of what you do.\nمَا كَانَ لِلْمُشْرِكِيْنَ اَنْ يَّعْمُرُوْا مَسٰجِدَ اللّٰهِ شٰهِدِيْنَ عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ بِالكُفْرِؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ ۖۚ وَ فِى النَّارِ هُمْ خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(17)\nMAA KAANA LIL-MUSHREKEENA AN-Y YA’MOROO MASAAJEDAL LAAHE SHAAHEDEENA A’LAA ANFOSEHIM BIL-KUFR, OOLAAA-EKA HABETAT A-A’MAALOHUM, WA FIN NAARE HUM KHAALEDOON.\nThe polytheists may not maintain Allah’s mosques while they are witness to their own unfaith. Their works have failed, and they shall remain in the Fire [forever].\nاِنَّمَا يَعْمُرُ مَسٰجِدَ اللّٰهِ مَنْ اٰمَنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَاَ قَامَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَى الزَّكٰوةَ وَلَمْ يَخْشَ اِلَّا اللّٰهَ فَعَسٰٓى اُولٰۤئِكَ اَنْ يَّكُوْنُوْا مِنَ الْمُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(18)\nINNAMAA YA’MORO MASAAJEDAL LAAHE MAN AAMANA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA AQAAMAS SALAATA WA AATAZ ZAKAATA WA LAM YAKHSHA ILLAL LAAHA FA-A’SAA OOLAAA-EKA AN-Y YAKOONOO MENAL MOHTADEEN.\nOnly those shall maintain Allah’s mosques who believe in Allah and the Last Day, and maintain the prayer, and give the zakat, and fear no one except Allah. They, hopefully, will be among the guided.\nاَجَعَلْتُمْ سِقَايَةَ الْحَآجِّ وَعِمَارَةَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ كَمَنْ اٰمَنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَجَاهَدَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ؕ لَا يَسْتَوٗنَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَ اللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۘ‏(19)\nAJA-A’LTUM SEQAAYATAL HAAJJE WA E’MAARATAL MASJEDIL HARAAME KAMAN AAMANA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA JAAHADA FEE SABEELIL LAAH, LAA YASTAWOONA I’NDAL LAAH, WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nDo you regard the providing of water to Hajj pilgrims and the maintenance of the Holy Mosque as similar [in worth] to someone who has faith in Allah and [believes in] the Last Day and wages jihad in the way of Allah? They are not equal with Allah, and Allah does not guide the wrongdoing lot.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ هَاجَرُوْا وَجَاهَدُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْۙ اَعْظَمُ دَرَجَةً عِنْدَ اللّٰهِؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْفَآئِزُوْنَ‏(20)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO WA HAAJAROO WA JAAHADOO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE BE-AMWAALEHIM WA ANFOSEHIM, A-A’ZAMO DARAJATAN I’NDAL LAAH, WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL FAAA-EZOON.\nThose who have believed and migrated, and waged jihad in the way of Allah with their possessions and persons have a greater rank near Allah, and it is they who are the triumphant.\nيُبَشِّرُهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنْهُ وَرِضْوَانٍ وَّجَنّٰتٍ لَّهُمْ فِيْهَا نَعِيْمٌ مُّقِيْمٌ ۙ‏(21)\nYOBASH-SHEROHUM RABBOHUM BE-RAHMATIM MINHO WA RIZWAANINW WA JANNAATIL LAHUM FEEHAA NA-E’EMUM MOQEEM.\nTheir Lord gives them the good news of His mercy and [His] pleasure, and for them there will be gardens with lasting bliss,\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عِنْدَهٗۤ اَجْرٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(22)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAA, INNAL LAAHA I’NDAHU AJRUN A’ZEEM.\nto remain in them forever. With Allah indeed is a great reward.\nيٰۤاَ يُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّخِذُوْۤا اٰبَآءَكُمْ وَاِخْوَانَكُمْ اَوْلِيَآءَ اِنِ اسْتَحَبُّوا الْكُفْرَ عَلَى الْاِيْمَانِ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّتَوَلَّهُمْ مِّنْكُمْ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(23)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TATTAKHEZOO AABAAA-AKUM WA IKHWAANAKUM AWLEYAAA-A ENIS TAHABBUL KUFRA A’LAL EEMAAN, WA MAN-Y YATAWALLAHUM MINKUM FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUZ ZAALEMOON.\nO you who have faith! Do not befriend your fathers and brothers if they prefer faithlessness to faith. Those of you who befriend them—it is they who are the wrongdoers.\nقُلْ اِنْ كَانَ اٰبَآؤُكُمْ وَاَبْنَآؤُكُمْ وَاِخْوَانُكُمْ وَاَزْوَاجُكُمْ وَعَشِيْرَتُكُمْ وَ اَمْوَالُ ۨاقْتَرَفْتُمُوْهَا وَتِجَارَةٌ تَخْشَوْنَ كَسَادَهَا وَ مَسٰكِنُ تَرْضَوْنَهَاۤ اَحَبَّ اِلَيْكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَ جِهَادٍ فِىْ سَبِيْلِهٖ فَتَرَ بَّصُوْا حَتّٰى يَاْتِىَ اللّٰهُ بِاَمْرِهٖ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(24)\nQUL IN KAANA AABAAA-OKUM WA ABNAAA-OKUM WA IKHWAANOKUM WA AZWAAJOKUM WA A’SHEERATOKUM WA AMWAALONIQ TARAFTOMOOHAA WA TEJAARATUN TAKHSHAWNA KASAADAHAA WA MASAAKENO TARZAWNAHAA AHABBA ELAYKUM MENAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WA JEHAADIN FEE SABEELEHI FA-TARABBASOO HATTAA YAATEYAL LAAHO BE-AMREH, WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAL FAASEQEEN.\nSay, ‘If your fathers and your sons, your brethren, your spouses, and your kinsfolk, the possessions that you have acquired, the business you fear may suffer, and the dwellings you are fond of, are dearer to you than Allah and His Apostle and to waging jihad in His way, then wait until Allah issues His edict, and Allah does not guide the transgressing lot.\nلَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللّٰهُ فِىْ مَوَاطِنَ كَثِيْرَةٍ ۙ وَّيَوْمَ حُنَيْنٍ ۙ اِذْ اَعْجَبَتْكُمْ كَثْرَتُكُمْ فَلَمْ تُغْنِ عَنْكُمْ شَيْئًا وَّضَاقَتْ عَلَيْكُمُ الْاَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ ثُمَّ وَلَّيْتُمْ مُّدْبِرِيْنَۚ‏(25)\nLAQAD NASARAKOMUL LAAHO FEE MAWAATENA KASEERATINW, WA YAWMA HONAYNIN, IZ A-A’JABATKUM KASRATOKUM FALAM TUGHNE A’NKUM SHAY-ANW WA ZAAQAT A’LAYKOMUL ARZO BEMAA RAHOBAT SUMMA WALLAYTUM MUDBEREEN.\nAllah has certainly helped you in many situations, and on the day of Hunayn, when your great number impressed you, but it did not avail you in any way, and the earth became narrow for you in spite of its expanse, whereupon you turned your backs [to flee].\nثُمَّ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ سَكِيْنَتَهٗ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِهٖ وَعَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَاَنْزَلَ جُنُوْدًا لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا ۚ وَعَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ جَزَآءُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(26)\nSUMMA ANZALAL LAAHO SAKEENATAHU A’LAA RASOOLEHI WA A’LAL MOAMENEENA WA ANZALA JONOODAL LAM TARAWHAA, WA A’ZZABAL LAZEENA KAFAROO, WA ZAALEKA JAZAAA-UL KAAFEREEN.\nThen Allah sent down His composure upon His Apostle and upon the faithful, and He sent down hosts you did not see, and He punished the faithless, and that is the requital of the faithless.\nثُمَّ يَتُوْبُ اللّٰهُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰ لِكَ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(27)\nSUMMA YATOOBUL LAAHO MIM BA’DE ZAALEKA A’LAA MAN-Y YASHAAA, WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nThen Allah shall turn clemently after that to whomever He wishes. Indeed Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّمَا الْمُشْرِكُوْنَ نَجَسٌ فَلَا يَقْرَبُوا الْمَسْجِدَ الْحَرَامَ بَعْدَ عَامِهِمْ هٰذَا ۚ وَ اِنْ خِفْتُمْ عَيْلَةً فَسَوْفَ يُغْنِيْكُمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖۤ اِنْ شَآءَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(28)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAMAL MUSHREKOONA NAJASUN FALAA YAQRABUL MASJEDAL HARAAMA BA’DA A’AMEHIM HAAZAA, WA IN KHIFTUM A’YLATAN FASAWFA YUGHNEEKOMUL LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI IN SHAAA, INNAL LAAHA A’LEEMUN HAKEEM.\nO you who have faith! The polytheists are indeed unclean: so let them not approach the Holy Mosque after this year. Should you fear poverty, Allah will enrich you out of His grace, if He wishes. Indeed Allah is all-knowing, all-wise.\nقَاتِلُوا الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَلَا بِالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَلَا يُحَرِّمُوْنَ مَا حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ وَ رَسُوْلُهٗ وَلَا يَدِيْنُوْنَ دِيْنَ الْحَقِّ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ حَتّٰى يُعْطُوا الْجِزْيَةَ عَنْ يَّدٍ وَّهُمْ صٰغِرُوْنَ‏(29)\nQAATELUL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WA LAA BIL-YAWMIL AAKHERE WA LAA YOHARREMOONA MAA HARRAMAL LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU WA LAA YADEENOONA DEENAL HAQQE MENAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA HATTAA YO’TUL JIZYATA A’N-Y YADINW WA HUM SAAGHEROON.\nFight those who do not have faith in Allah nor [believe] in the Last Day, nor forbid what Allah and His Apostle have forbidden, nor practise the true religion, from among those who were given the Book, until they pay the tribute out of hand, degraded.\nوَقَالَتِ الْيَهُوْدُ عُزَيْرُ ۨابْنُ اللّٰهِ وَقَالَتِ النَّصٰرَى الْمَسِيْحُ ابْنُ اللّٰهِؕ ذٰ لِكَ قَوْلُهُمْ بِاَ فْوَاهِهِمْ ۚ يُضَاهِئُونَ قَوْلَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ ؕ قَاتَلَهُمُ اللّٰهُ ۚ اَنّٰى يُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏‏(30)\nWA QAALATIL YAHOODO O’ZAYRONIB NUL LAAHE WA QAALATIN NASAARAL MASEEHUB NUL LAAH, ZAALEKA QAWLOHUM BE-AFWAAHEHIM, YOZAAHE-OONA QAWLAL LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QABL, QAATALAHOMUL LAAH, ANNAA YOAFAKOON.\nThe Jews say, ‘Ezra is the son of Allah,’ and the Christians say, ‘Christ is the son of Allah.’ That is an opinion that they mouth, imitating the opinions of the faithless of former times. May Allah assail them, where do they stray?!\nاِتَّخَذُوْۤا اَحْبَارَهُمْ وَرُهْبَانَهُمْ اَرْبَابًا مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَالْمَسِيْحَ ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ ۚ وَمَاۤ اُمِرُوْۤا اِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلٰهًا وَّاحِدًا ۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(31)\nITTAKHAZOO AHBAARAHUM WA ROHBAANAHUM ARBAABAM MIN DOONIL LAAHE WAL MASEEHAB NA MARYAM, WA MAA OMEROO ILLAA LE-YA’BODOO ELAAHANW WAAHEDAA, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO, SUBHAANAHU A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nThey have taken their scribes and their monks as lords besides Allah, and also Christ, Mary’s son; though they were commanded to worship only the One God, there is no god except Him; He is far too immaculate to have any partners that they ascribe [to Him]!\nيُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يُّطْفِئُوْا نُوْرَ اللّٰهِ بِاَ فْوَاهِهِمْ وَيَاْبَى اللّٰهُ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّتِمَّ نُوْرَهٗ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(32)\nYOREEDOONA AN-Y YUTFE-OO NOORAL LAAHE BE-AFWAAHEHIM WA YAABAL LAAHO ILLAA AN-Y YOTIMMA NOORAHU WA LAW KAREHAL KAAFEROON.\nThey desire to put out the light of Allah with their mouths, but Allah is intent on perfecting His light though the faithless should be averse.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَرْسَلَ رَسُوْلَهٗ بِالْهُدٰى وَدِيْنِ الْحَقِّ لِيُظْهِرَهٗ عَلَى الدِّيْنِ كُلِّهٖۙ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْمُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(33)\nHOWAL LAZEE ARSALA RASOOLAHU BIL-HODAA WA DEENIL HAQQE LE-YUZHERAHU A’LAD DEENE KULLEHI, WA LAW KAREHAL MUSHREKOON.\nIt is He who has sent His Apostle with the guidance and the religion of truth that He may make it prevail over all religions, though the polytheists should be averse.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ الْاَحْبَارِ وَالرُّهْبَانِ لَيَاْكُلُوْنَ اَمْوَالَ النَّاسِ بِالْبَاطِلِ وَيَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يَكْنِزُوْنَ الذَّهَبَ وَالْفِضَّةَ وَلَا يُنْفِقُوْنَهَا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِۙ فَبَشِّرْهُمْ بِعَذَابٍ اَلِيْمٍۙ‏(34)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNA KASEERAM MENAL AHBAARE WAR ROHBAANE LAYAAKOLOONA AMWAALAN NAASE BIL-BAATELE WA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAH, WAL LAZEENA YAKNEZOONAZ ZAHABA WAL FIZZATA WA LAA YUNFEQOONAHAA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE, FA-BASH-SHIRHUM BE-A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\nO you who have faith! Indeed many of the scribes and monks wrongfully eat up the people’s wealth, and bar [them] from the way of Allah. Those who treasure up gold and silver, and do not spend it in the way of Allah, inform them of a painful punishment\nيَّومَ يُحْمٰى عَلَيْهَا فِىْ نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ فَتُكْوٰى بِهَا جِبَاهُهُمْ وَجُنُوْبُهُمْ وَظُهُوْرُهُمْؕ هٰذَا مَا كَنَزْتُمْ لِاَنْفُسِكُمْ فَذُوْقُوْا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْنِزُوْنَ‏(35)\nYAWMA YOHMAA A’LAYHAA FEE NAARE JAHANNAMA FA-TUKWAA BEHAA JEBAAHOHUM WA JONOOBOHUM WA ZOHOOROHUM, HAAZAA MAA KANAZTUM LE-ANFOSEKUM FA-ZOOQOO MAA KUNTUM TAKNEZOON.\non the day when these shall be heated in hellfire and therewith branded on their foreheads, their sides, and their backs [and told]: ‘This is what you treasured up for yourselves! So taste what you have treasured!’\nاِنَّ عِدَّةَ الشُّهُوْرِ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ اثْنَا عَشَرَ شَهْرًا فِىْ كِتٰبِ اللّٰهِ يَوْمَ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ مِنْهَاۤ اَرْبَعَةٌ حُرُمٌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الدِّيْنُ الْقَيِّمُ ۙ فَلَا تَظْلِمُوْا فِيْهِنَّ اَنْفُسَكُمْ ؕ وَقَاتِلُوا الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ كَآفَّةً كَمَا يُقَاتِلُوْنَكُمْ كَآفَّةً  ؕ وَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(36)\nINNA I’DDATASH SHOHOORE I’NDAL LAAHIS NAA A’SHARA SHAHRAN FEE KETAABIL LAAHE YAWMA KHALAQAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA MINHAA ARBA-A’TUN HOROM, ZAALEKAD DEENUL QAYYEMO, FALAA TAZLEMOO FEEHINNA ANFOSAKUM, WA QAATELUL MUSHREKEENA KAAFFATAN KAMAA YOQAATELOONAKUM KAAFFAH, WA’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nIndeed the number of months with Allah is twelve months in Allah’s Book, the day when He created the heavens and the earth. Of these, four are sacred. That is the upright religion. So do not wrong yourselves during them. Fight all the polytheists, just as they fight you all, and know that Allah is with the Godwary.\nاِنَّمَا النَّسِىْٓءُ زِيَادَةٌ فِى الْكُفْرِ يُضَلُّ بِهِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُحِلُّوْنَهٗ عَامًا وَّيُحَرِّمُوْنَهٗ عَامًا لِّيُوَاطِئُوْا عِدَّةَ مَا حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ فَيُحِلُّوْا مَا حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ ؕ زُيِّنَ لَهُمْ سُوْۤءُ اَعْمَالِهِمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(37)\nINNAMAN NASEE-O ZEYAADATUN FIL KUFRE YOZALLO BEHIL LAZEENA KAFAROO YOHILLOONAHU A’AMANW WA YOHARREMOONAHU A’AMAL LE-YOWAATE-OO I’DDATA MAA HARRAMAL LAAHO FA-YOHILLOO MAA HARRAMAL LAAH, ZUYYENA LAHUM SOO-O A-A’MAALEHIM, WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAL KAAFEREEN.\nIndeed nasee is an increase in unfaith, whereby the faithless are led [further] astray. They allow it in one year and forbid it another year, so as to fit in with the number, which Allah has made inviolable, thus permitting what Allah has forbidden. Their evil deeds appear to them as decorous, and Allah does not guide the faithless lot.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَا لَكُمْ اِذَا قِيْلَ لَكُمُ انْفِرُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ اثَّاقَلْتُمْ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ ؕ اَرَضِيْتُمْ بِالْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا مِنَ الْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ فَمَا مَتَاعُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ اِلَّا قَلِيْلٌ‏(38)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MAA LAKUM EZAA QEELA LAKOMUN FEROO FEE SABEELIL LAAHIS SAAQALTUM ELAL ARZ, ARAZEETUM BIL-HAYAATID DUNYAA MENAL AAKHERAH, FAMAA MATAA-U’L HAYAATID DUNYAA FIL AAKHERATE ILLAA QALEEL.\nO you who have faith! What is the matter with you that when you are told: ‘Go forth in the way of Allah,’ you sink heavily to the ground? Are you pleased with the life of this world instead of the Hereafter? But the wares of the life of this world compared with the Hereafter are but insignificant.\nاِلَّا تَنْفِرُوْا يُعَذِّبْكُمْ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًا   ۙ وَّيَسْتَبْدِلْ قَوْمًا غَيْرَكُمْ وَلَا تَضُرُّوْهُ شَيْئًا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(39)\nILLAA TANFEROO YO-A’ZZIBKUM A’ZAABAN ALEEMANW, WA YASTABDIL QAWMAN GHAYRAKUM WA LAA TAZURROOHO SHAY-AA, WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nIf you do not go forth, He will punish you with a painful punishment, and replace you with another people, and you will not hurt Him in the least, and Allah has power over all things.\nاِلَّا تَنْصُرُوْهُ فَقَدْ نَصَرَهُ اللّٰهُ اِذْ اَخْرَجَهُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ثَانِىَ اثْنَيْنِ اِذْ هُمَا فِى الْغَارِ اِذْ يَقُوْلُ لِصَاحِبِهٖ لَا تَحْزَنْ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَنَا ۚ فَاَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ سَكِيْنَتَهٗ عَلَيْهِ وَاَ يَّدَهٗ بِجُنُوْدٍ لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا وَجَعَلَ كَلِمَةَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوا السُّفْلٰى ؕ وَكَلِمَةُ اللّٰهِ هِىَ الْعُلْيَا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(40)\nILLAA TANSOROOHO FAQAD NASARAHUL LAAHO IZ AKHRAJAHUL LAZEENA KAFAROO SAANEYAS NAYNE IZ HOMAA FIL GHAARE IZ YAQOOLO LE-SAAHEBEHI LAA TAHZAN INNAL LAAHA MA-A’NAA, FA-ANZALAL LAAHO SAKEENATAHU A’LAYHE WA AYYADAHU BE-JONOODIL LAM TARAWHAA WA JA-A’LA KALEMATAL LAZEENA KAFARUS SUFLAA, WA KALEMATUL LAAHE HEYAL U’LYAA, WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nIf you do not help him, then Allah certainly helped him when the faithless expelled him, as one of two [refugees], when the two of them were in the cave, he said to his companion, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is indeed with us.’ Then Allah sent down His composure upon him, and strengthened him with hosts you did not see, and He made the word of the faithless the lowest; and the word of Allah is the highest; and Allah is all-mighty, all-wise.\nاِنْفِرُوْا خِفَافًا وَّثِقَالًا وَّجَاهِدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِكُمْ وَاَنْفُسِكُمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(41)\nINFEROO KHEFAAFANW WA SEQAALANW WA JAAHEDOO BE-AMWAALEKUM WA ANFOSEKUM FEE SABEELIL LAAH, ZAALEKUM KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nGo forth, whether [armed] lightly or heavily, and wage jihad with your possessions and persons in the way of Allah. That is better for you, should you know.\nلَوْ كَانَ عَرَضًا قَرِيْبًا وَّسَفَرًا قَاصِدًا لَّاتَّبَعُوْكَ وَلٰكِنْۢ بَعُدَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الشُّقَّةُ  ؕ وَسَيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ لَوِ اسْتَطَعْنَا لَخَرَجْنَا مَعَكُمْ ۚ يُهْلِكُوْنَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ ۚ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ اِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(42)\nLAW KAANA A’RAZAN QAREEBANW WA SAFARAN QAASEDAL LATTABA-O’OKA WA LAAKIM BA-O’DAT A’LAYHEMUSH SHUQQAH, WA SAYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE LAWIS TATA’NAA LAKHARAJNAA MA-A’KUM, YOHLEKOONA ANFOSAHUM, WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nWere it an accessible gain or a short journey, they would have surely followed you; but the distance seemed too far to them. Yet they will swear by Allah: ‘If we could, we would have surely gone forth with you.’ They [merely] destroy themselves. Allah knows that they are indeed liars.\nعَفَا اللّٰهُ عَنْكَۚ لِمَ اَذِنْتَ لَهُمْ حَتّٰى يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكَ الَّذِيْنَ صَدَقُوْا وَتَعْلَمَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(43)\nA’FAL LAAHO A’NK, LEMA AZINTA LAHUM HATTAA YATABAYYANA LAKAL LAZEENA SADAQOO WA TA’LAMAL KAAZEBEEN.\nMay Allah excuse you! Why did you grant them leave [to stay behind] before those who told the truth were evident to you and you had ascertained the liars?\nلَا يَسْتَاْذِنُكَ الَّذِيْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ اَنْ يُّجَاهِدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِالْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(44)\nLAA YASTAAZENOKAL LAZEENA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE AN-Y YOJAAHEDOO BE-AMWAALEHIM WA ANFOSEHIM, WAL LAAHO A’LEEMUM BIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nThose who believe in Allah and the Last Day do not ask you for leave [exempting them] from waging jihad with their possessions and their persons, and Allah knows best the Godwary.\nاِنَّمَا يَسْتَاْذِنُكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَارْتَابَتْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ فَهُمْ فِىْ رَيْبِهِمْ يَتَرَدَّدُوْنَ‏(45)\nINNAMAA YASTAAZENOKAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WAR TAABAT QOLOOBOHUM FAHUM FEE RAYBEHIM YATARADDADOON.\nOnly those seek a leave [of exemption] from you who do not believe in Allah and the Last Day, and whose hearts are in doubt, so they waver in their doubt.\nوَلَوْ اَرَادُوْا الْخُرُوْجَ لَاَعَدُّوْا لَهٗ عُدَّةً وَّلٰكِنْ كَرِهَ اللّٰهُ انۢبِعَاثَهُمْ فَثَبَّطَهُمْ وَقِيْلَ اقْعُدُوْا مَعَ الْقٰعِدِيْنَ‏(46)\nWA LAW ARAADUL KHOROOJA LA-A-A’DDOO LAHU U’DDATANW WA LAAKIN KAREHAL LAAHUM BE-A’ASAHUM FA-SABBATAHUM WA QEELAQ O’DOO MA-A’L QAA-E’DEEN.\nHad they desired to go forth, they would have surely made some preparations for it; but Allah was averse to arouse them, so He held them back, and it was said [to them], ‘Be seated with those who sit back.’\nلَوْ خَرَجُوْا فِيْكُمْ مَّا زَادُوْكُمْ اِلَّا خَبَالًا وَّلَاْاَوْضَعُوْا خِلٰلَكُمْ يَبْغُوْنَكُمُ الْفِتْنَةَ ۚ وَفِيْكُمْ سَمّٰعُوْنَ لَهُمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِالظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(47)\nLAW KHARAJOO FEEKUM MAA ZAADOOKUM ILLAA KHABAALANW WA LA-AWZA-O’O KHELAALAKUM YABGHOONAKOMUL FITNAH, WA FEEKUM SAMMAA-O’ONA LAHUM, WAL LAAHO A’LEEMUM BIZ-ZAALEMEEN.\nHad they gone forth with you, they would have only added to your troubles, and they would have surely spread rumours in your midst, seeking to cause sedition among you. They have some spies among you, and Allah knows best the wrongdoers.\nلَقَدِ ابْتَغَوُا الْفِتْنَةَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَقَلَّبُوْا لَكَ الْاُمُوْرَ حَتّٰى جَآءَ الْحَقُّ وَظَهَرَ اَمْرُ اللّٰهِ وَهُمْ كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(48)\nLAQADIB TAGHAWUL FITNATA MIN QABLO WA QALLABOO LAKAL OMOORA HATTAA JAAA-AL HAQQO WA ZAHARA AMRUL LAAHE WA HUM KAAREHOON.\nThey certainly sought to cause sedition earlier, and upset the matters for you, until the truth came and Allah’s command prevailed, much as they were averse.\nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّقُوْلُ ائْذَنْ لِّىْ وَلَا تَفْتِنِّىْ ؕ اَلَا فِى الْفِتْنَةِ سَقَطُوْا ؕ وَاِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ لَمُحِيْطَةٌ ۢ بِالْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(49)\nWA MINHUM MAN-Y YAQOOLOAZAL LEE WA LAA TAFTINNEE, ALAA FIL FITNATE SAQATOO, WA INNA JAHANNAMA LA-MOHEETATUM BIL-KAAFEREEN.\nAmong them there are some who say, ‘Give me leave, and do not put me to temptation.’ Look! They have already fallen into temptation and indeed hell besieges the faithless.\nاِنْ تُصِبْكَ حَسَنَةٌ تَسُؤْهُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ تُصِبْكَ مُصِيْبَةٌ يَّقُوْلُوْا قَدْ اَخَذْنَاۤ اَمْرَنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَيَتَوَلَّوْا وَّهُمْ فَرِحُوْنَ‏(50)\nIN TOSIBKA HASANATUN TASOAHUM, WA IN TOSIBKA MOSEEBATUN-Y YAQOOLOO QAD AKHAZNAA AMRANAA MIN QABLO WA YATAWALLAW WA HUM FAREHOON.\nIf some good should befall you, it upsets them; but if an adversity befalls you, they say, ‘We had already taken our precautions in advance,’ and they go away boasting.\nقُلْ لَّنْ يُّصِيْبَنَاۤ اِلَّا مَا كَتَبَ اللّٰهُ لَنَا ۚ هُوَ مَوْلٰٮنَا  ۚ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(51)\nQUL LAN-Y YOSEEBANAA ILLAA MAA KATABAL LAAHO LANAA, HOWA MAWLAANAA, WA A’LAL LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALIL MOAMENOON.\nSay, ‘Nothing will befall us except what Allah has ordained for us. He is our master, and in Allah let all the faithful put their trust.’\nقُلْ هَلْ تَرَبَّصُوْنَ بِنَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اِحْدَى الْحُسْنَيَيْنِؕ وَنَحْنُ نَتَرَبَّصُ بِكُمْ اَنْ يُّصِيْبَكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِعَذَابٍ مِّنْ عِنْدِهٖۤ اَوْ بِاَيْدِيْنَا  ۖ  فَتَرَبَّصُوْۤا اِنَّا مَعَكُمْ مُّتَرَبِّصُوْنَ‏(52)\nQUL HAL TARABBASOONA BENAA ILLAA EHDAL HUSNAYAYN, WA NAHNO NATARABBASO BEKUM AN-Y YOSEEBAKOMUL LAAHO BE-A’ZAABIM MIN I’NDEHI AW BE-AYDEENAA, FA-TARABBASOO INNAA MA-A’KUM MOTARABBESOON.\nSay, ‘Do you not await one of the two excellent things to happen to us? But we await that Allah shall visit on you a punishment, from Him, or by our hands. So wait! We too are waiting along with you.’\nقُلْ اَنْفِقُوْا طَوْعًا اَوْ كَرْهًا لَّنْ يُّتَقَبَّلَ مِنْكُمْؕ اِنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏(53)\nQUL ANFEQOO TAW-A’N AW KARHAL LAN-Y YOTAQABBALA MINKUM, INNAKUM KUNTUM QAWMAN FAASEQEEN.\nSay, ‘Spend willingly or unwillingly, it shall never be accepted from you; for you are indeed a transgressing lot.’\nوَمَا مَنَعَهُمْ اَنْ تُقْبَلَ مِنْهُمْ نَفَقٰتُهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَبِرَسُوْلِهٖ وَلَا يَاْتُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ اِلَّا وَهُمْ كُسَالٰى وَلَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ اِلَّا وَهُمْ كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(54)\nWA MAA MANA-A’HUM AN TUQBALA MINHUM NAFAQAATOHUM ILLAA ANNAHUM KAFAROO BIL-LAAHE WA BE-RASOOLEHI WA LAA YAATOONAS SALAATA ILLAA WA HUM KOSAALAA WA LAA YUNFEQOONA ILLAA WA HUM KAAREHOON.\nNothing stops their charities from being accepted except that they have no faith in Allah and His Apostle and do not perform the prayer but lazily, and do not spend but reluctantly.\nفَلَا تُعْجِبْكَ اَمْوَالُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَوْلَادُهُمْؕ اِنَّمَا يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ لِيُعَذِّبَهُمْ بِهَا فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَتَزْهَقَ اَنْفُسُهُمْ وَهُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(55)\nFALAA TO’JIBKA AMWAALOHUM WA LAA AWLAADOHUM, INNAMAA YOREEDUL LAAHO LE-YO-A’ZZEBAHUM BEHAA FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA TAZHAQA ANFOSOHUM WA HUM KAAFEROON.\nSo let not their wealth and children impress you: Allah only desires to punish them with these in the life of this world, and that their souls may depart while they are faithless.\nوَيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ اِنَّهُمْ لَمِنْكُمْؕ وَمَا هُمْ مِّنْكُمْ وَلٰكِنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ يَّفْرَقُوْنَ‏(56)\nWA YAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE INNAHUM LAMINKUM, WA MAA HUM MINKUM WA LAAKINNAHUM QAWMUN-Y YAFRAQOON.\nThey swear by Allah that they belong to you, but they do not belong to you. Rather, they are a frightened lot.\nلَوْ يَجِدُوْنَ مَلْجَاً اَوْ مَغٰرٰتٍ اَوْ مُدَّخَلًا لَّوَلَّوْا اِلَيْهِ وَهُمْ يَجْمَحُوْنَ‏(57)\nLAW YAJEDOONA MALJA-AN AW MAGHAARAATIN AW MUDDAKHALAL LAWALLAW ELAYHE WA HUM YAJMAHOON.\nIf they could find a refuge, or a hideout, or a hole [to creep into], they would turn to it in frantic haste.\nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّلْمِزُكَ فِى الصَّدَقٰتِ ۚ فَاِنْ اُعْطُوْا مِنْهَا رَضُوْا وَاِنْ لَّمْ يُعْطَوْا مِنْهَاۤ اِذَا هُمْ يَسْخَطُوْنَ‏(58)\nWA MINHUM MAN-Y YALMEZOKA FIS SADAQAAT, FA-IN O-O’TOO MINHAA RAZOO WA IL LAM YO’TAW MINHAA EZAA HUM YASKHATOON.\nThere are some of them who blame you regarding [the distribution of] the charities: if they are given from them, they are pleased, but if they are not given from them, behold, they are displeased.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ رَضُوْا مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗۙ وَقَالُوْا حَسْبُنَا اللّٰهُ سَيُؤْتِيْنَا اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ وَ رَسُوْلُهٗۙ اِنَّاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ رٰغِبُوْنَ‏(59)\nWA LAW ANNAHUM RAZOO MAA AATAAHOMUL LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU, WA QAALOO HASBONAL LAAHO SAYOATEENAL LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI WA RASOOLOHU, INNAA ELAL LAAHE RAAGHEBOON.\n[It would have been better] if they had been pleased with what Allah and His Apostle gave them, and had said, ‘Allah is sufficient for us; Allah and His Apostle will give to us out of His grace. Indeed to Allah do we eagerly turn.’\nاِنَّمَا الصَّدَقٰتُ لِلْفُقَرَآءِ وَالْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَالْعٰمِلِيْنَ عَلَيْهَا وَالْمُؤَلَّفَةِ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَفِى الرِّقَابِ وَالْغٰرِمِيْنَ وَفِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيْلِؕ فَرِيْضَةً مِّنَ اللّٰهِؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(60)\nINNAMAS SADAQAATO LIL-FOQARAAA-E WAL MASAAKEENE WAL A’AMELEENA A’LAYHAA WAL MO-ALLAFATE QOLOOBOHUM WA FIR REQAABE WAL GHAAREMEENA WA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WAB NIS SABEEL, FAREEZATAM MENAL LAAH, WAL LAAHO A’LEEMUN HAKEEM.\nThe charities are only for the poor and the needy, and those employed to collect them, and those whose hearts are to be reconciled, and for [the freedom of] the slaves and the debtors, and in the way of Allah, and for the traveller. [This is] an ordinance from Allah, and Allah is all-knowing, all-wise.\nوَمِنْهُمُ الَّذِيْنَ يُؤْذُوْنَ النَّبِىَّ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ هُوَ اُذُنٌ ؕ قُلْ اُذُنُ خَيْرٍ لَّكُمْ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَيُؤْمِنُ لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَرَحْمَةٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مِنْكُمْ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يُؤْذُوْنَ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(61)\nWA MINHOMUL LAZEENA YOAZOONAN NABIYYA WA YAQOOLOONA HOWA OZON, QUL OZONO KHAYRIL LAKUM YOAMENO BIL-LAAHE WA YOAMENO LIL-MOAMENEENA WA RAHMATUL LILLAZEENA AAMANOO MINKUM, WAL LAZEENA YOAZOONA RASOOLAL LAAHE LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nAmong them are those who torment the Prophet, and say, ‘He is an ear.’ Say, ‘An ear that is good for you. He has faith in Allah and trusts the faithful, and is a mercy for those of you who have faith.’ As for those who torment the Apostle of Allah, there is a painful punishment for them.\nيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ لَكُمْ لِيُرْضُوْكُمْۚ وَاللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗۤ اَحَقُّ اَنْ يُّرْضُوْهُ اِنْ كَانُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(62)\nYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE LAKUM LE-YURZOOKUM, WAL LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU AHAQQO AN-Y YURZOOHO IN KAANOO MOAMENEEN.\nThey swear to you by Allah, to please you; but Allah and His Apostle are worthier that they should please Him, should they be faithful.\nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّهٗ مَنْ يُّحَادِدِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ فَاَنَّ لَهٗ نَارَ جَهَنَّمَ خَالِدًا فِيْهَا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْخِزْىُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(63)\nALAM YA’LAMOO ANNAHU MAN-Y YOHAADEDIL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU FA-ANNA LAHU NAARA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDAN FEEHAA, ZAALEKAL KHIZYUL A’ZEEM.\nDo they not know that whoever opposes Allah and His Apostle, there awaits him the Fire of hell, to remain in it [forever]? That is the great disgrace.\nيَحْذَرُ الْمُنٰفِقُوْنَ اَنْ تُنَزَّلَ عَلَيْهِمْ سُوْرَةٌ تُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ ؕ قُلِ اسْتَهْزِءُوْا ۚ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ مُخْرِجٌ مَّا تَحْذَرُوْنَ‏(64)\nYAHZARUL MONAAFEQOONA AN TONAZZALA A’LAYHIM SOORATUN TONABBE-OHUM BEMAA FEE QOLOOBEHIM, QOLIS TAHZE-OO, INNAL LAAHA MUKHREJUM MAA TAHZAROON.\nThe hypocrites are apprehensive lest a surah should be sent down against them, informing them about what is in their hearts. Say, ‘Go on deriding. Allah will indeed bring out what you are apprehensive of.’\nوَلَئِنْ سَاَلْتَهُمْ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اِنَّمَا كُنَّا نَخُوْضُ وَنَلْعَبُؕ قُلْ اَبِاللّٰهِ وَاٰيٰتِهٖ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ كُنْتُمْ تَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(65)\nWA LA-IN SA-ALTAHUM LAYAQOOLUNNA INNAMAA KUNNAA NAKHOOZO WA NAL-A’B, QUL ABIL-LAAHE WA AAYAATEHI WA RASOOLEHI KUNTUM TASTAHZE-OON.\nIf you question them [regarding their conduct], they will surely say, ‘We were just gossiping and amusing ourselves.’ Say, ‘Were you deriding Allah, His signs, and His apostles?\nلَا تَعْتَذِرُوْا قَدْ كَفَرْتُمْ بَعْدَ اِيْمَانِكُمْ ؕ اِنْ نَّعْفُ عَنْ طَآئِفَةٍ مِّنْكُمْ نُعَذِّبْ طَآئِفَةً ۢ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا مُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(66)\nLAA TA’TAZEROO QAD KAFARTUM BA’DA EEMAANEKUM, IN NA’FO A’N TAAA-EFATIM MINKUM NO-A’ZZIB TAAA-EFATAM BE-ANNAHUM KAANOO MUJREMEEN.\nDo not make excuses. You have disbelieved after your faith.’ If We forgive a group among you, We will punish another group, for they have been guilty.\nاَلْمُنٰفِقُوْنَ وَالْمُنٰفِقٰتُ بَعْضُهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْضٍۘ يَاْمُرُوْنَ بِالْمُنْكَرِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمَعْرُوْفِ وَيَقْبِضُوْنَ اَيْدِيَهُمْؕ نَسُوا اللّٰهَ فَنَسِيَهُمْؕ اِنَّ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ هُمُ الْفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(67)\nAL-MONAAFEQOONA WAL MONAAFEQAATO BA’ZOHUM MIM BA’Z, YAAMOROONA BIL-MUNKARE WA YANHAWNA A’NIL MA’ROOFE WA YAQBEZOONA AYDEYAHUM, NASUL LAAHA FA-NASEYAHUM, INNAL MONAAFEQEENA HOMUL FAASEQOON.\nThe hypocrites, men and women, are all alike: they bid what is wrong and forbid what is right; and are tight-fisted. They have forgotten Allah, so He has forgotten them. The hypocrites are indeed the transgressors.\nوَعَدَ اللّٰهُ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ وَالْمُنٰفِقٰتِ وَالْكُفَّارَ نَارَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ هِىَ حَسْبُهُمْ ۚ وَلَعَنَهُمُ اللّٰهُ ۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّقِيْمٌ ۙ‏(68)\nWA-A’DAL LAAHUL MONAAFEQEENA WAL MONAAFEQAATE WAL KUFFAARA NAARA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, HEYA HASBOHUM, WA LA-A’NAHOMUL LAAH, WA LAHUM A’ZAABUM MOQEEM.\nAllah has promised the hypocrites, men and women, and the faithless, the Fire of hell, to remain in it [forever]. That suffices them. Allah has cursed them, and there is a lasting punishment for them.\nكَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ كَانُوْۤا اَشَدَّ مِنْكُمْ قُوَّةً وَّاَكْثَرَ اَمْوَالًا وَّاَوْلَادًا ؕ فَاسْتَمْتَعُوْا بِخَلَاقِهِمْ فَاسْتَمْتَعْتُمْ بِخَلَاقِكُمْ كَمَا اسْتَمْتَعَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ بِخَلَاقِهِمْ وَخُضْتُمْ كَالَّذِىْ خَاضُوْا ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(69)\nKALLAZEENA MIN QABLEKUM KAANOO ASHADDA MINKUM QUWWATANW WA AKSARA AMWAALANW WA AWLAADAA, FASTAMTA-O’O BE-KHALAAQEHIM FASTAMTA’TUM BE-KHALAAQEKUM KAMAS TAMTA-A’L LAZEENA MIN QABLEKUM BE-KHALAAQEHIM WA KHUZTUM KALLAZEE KHAAZOO, OOLAAA-EKA HABETAT A-A’MAALOHUM FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH, WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\n[Hypocrites! Your case is] similar to those who were before you, who were more powerful than you and more abounding in wealth and children: they enjoyed their share [of worldly existence]; you too enjoy your share, just like those who were before you enjoyed their share, and you have gossiped [impiously] as they gossiped. They are the ones whose works have failed in this world and the Hereafter; and it is they who are the losers.\nاَلَمْ يَاْتِهِمْ نَبَاُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ قَوْمِ نُوْحٍ وَّعَادٍ وَّثَمُوْدَ  ۙ وَقَوْمِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاَصْحٰبِ مَدْيَنَ وَالْمُؤْتَفِكٰتِ ؕ اَتَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ ۚ فَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيَظْلِمَهُمْ وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(70)\nALAM YAATEHIM NABA-UL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM QAWME NOOHINW WA A’ADINW WA SAMOODA, WA QAWME IBRAAHEEMA WA ASHAABE MADYANA WAL MOATAFEKAAT, ATATHUM ROSOLOHUM BIL-BAYYENAAT, FAMAA KAANAL LAAHO LE-YAZLEMAHUM WA LAAKIN KAANOO ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nHas there not come to them the account of those who were before them—the people of Noah, ‘Ad, and Tham£d, and the people of Abraham, the inhabitants of Midian, and the towns that were overturned? Their apostles brought them manifest proofs. So it was not Allah who wronged them, but it was they who used to wrong themselves.\nوَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنٰتُ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍۘ يَاْمُرُوْنَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَيُقِيْمُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَيُطِيْعُوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ سَيَرْحَمُهُمُ اللّٰهُؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(71)\nWAL MOAMENOONA WAL MOAMENAATO BA’ZOHUM AWLEYAAA-O BA’Z, YAAMOROONA BIL-MA’ROOFE WA YANHAWNA A’NIL MUNKARE WA YOQEEMOONAS SALAATA WA YOATOONAZ ZAKAATA WA YOTEE-O’ONAL LAAHA WA RASOOLAH, OOLAAA-EKA SAYARHAMOHOMUL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nBut the faithful, men and women, are comrades of one another: they bid what is right and forbid what is wrong and maintain the prayer, give the zakat, and obey Allah and His Apostle. It is they to whom Allah will soon grant His mercy. Indeed Allah is all-mighty, all-wise.\nوَعَدَ اللّٰهُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنٰتِ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا وَمَسٰكِنَ طَيِّبَةً فِىْ جَنّٰتِ عَدْنٍ ؕ وَرِضْوَانٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ اَكْبَرُ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(72)\nWA-A’DAL LAAHUL MOAMENEENA WAL MOAMENAATE JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WA MASAAKENA TAYYEBATAN FEE JANNAATE A’DN, WA RIZWAANUM MENAL LAAHE AKBAR, ZAALEKA HOWAL FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nAllah has promised the faithful, men and women, gardens with streams running in them, to remain in them [forever], and good dwellings in the Gardens of Eden. Yet Allah’s pleasure is greater [than all these]; that is the great success.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ جَاهِدِ الْكُفَّارَ وَالْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ وَاغْلُظْ عَلَيْهِمْؕ وَ مَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(73)\nYAA AYYOHAN NABIYYO JAAHEDIL KUFFAARA WAL MONAAFEQEENA WAGH LUZ A’LAYHIM, WA MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM, WA BEASAL MASEER.\nO Prophet! Wage jihad against the faithless and the hypocrites, and be severe with them. Their refuge shall be hell, and it is an evil destination.\nيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ مَا قَالُوْا ؕ وَلَقَدْ قَالُوْا كَلِمَةَ الْكُفْرِ وَكَفَرُوْا بَعْدَ اِسْلَامِهِمْ وَهَمُّوْا بِمَا لَمْ يَنَالُوْا ۚ وَمَا نَقَمُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اَنْ اَغْنٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ ۚ فَاِنْ يَّتُوْبُوْا يَكُ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ يَّتَوَلَّوْا يُعَذِّبْهُمُ اللّٰهُ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًا ۙ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ وَمَا لَهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(74)\nYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE MAA QAALOO, WA LAQAD QAALOO KALEMATAL KUFRE WA KAFAROO BA’DA ISLAAMEHIM WA HAMMOO BEMAA LAM YANAALOO, WA MAA NAQAMOO ILLAA AN AGHNAAHOMUL LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU MIN FAZLEH, FA-IN-Y YATOOBOO YAKO KHAYRAL LAHUM, WA IN-Y YATAWALLAW YO-A’ZZIBHOMUL LAAHO A’ZAABAN ALEEMAN, FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH, WA MAA LAHUM FIL ARZE MINW WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nThey swear by Allah that they did not say it. But they certainly did utter the word of unfaith and renounced faith after their Islam. They contemplated what they could not achieve, and they were vindictive only because Allah and His Apostle had enriched them out of His grace. Yet if they repent, it will be better for them; but if they turn away, Allah shall punish them with a painful punishment in this world and the Hereafter, and they shall not find on the earth any guardian or helper.\nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ عَاهَدَ اللّٰهَ لَئِنْ اٰتٰٮنَا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ لَنَصَّدَّقَنَّ وَلَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(75)\nWA MINHUM MAN A’AHADAL LAAHA LA-IN AATAANAA MIN FAZLEHI LANASSADDAQANNA WA LANAKOONANNA MENAS SAALEHEEN.\nAmong them are those who made a pledge with Allah: ‘If He gives us out of His grace, we will surely give the zakat and we will surely be among the righteous.’\nفَلَمَّاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمْ مِّنْ فَضْلِهٖ بَخِلُوْا بِهٖ وَتَوَلَّوْا وَّهُمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(76)\nFALAMMAA AATAAHUM MIN FAZLEHI BAKHELOO BEHI WA TAWALLAW WA HUM MO’REZOON.\nBut when He gave them out of His grace, they begrudged it and turned away, being disregardful.\nفَاَعْقَبَهُمْ نِفَاقًا فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يَلْقَوْنَهٗ بِمَاۤ اَخْلَفُوا اللّٰهَ مَا وَعَدُوْهُ وَبِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْذِبُوْنَ‏(77)\nFA-A-A’QABAHUM NEFAAQAN FEE QOLOOBEHIM ELAA YAWME YALQAWNAHU BEMAA AKHLAFUL LAAHA MAA WA-A’DOOHO WA BEMAA KAANOO YAKZEBOON.\nSo He caused hypocrisy to ensue in their hearts until the day they will encounter Him, because of their going back on what they had promised Allah and because of the lies they used to tell.\nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ سِرَّهُمْ وَنَجْوٰٮهُمْ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوْبِ ۚ‏(78)\nALAM YA’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO SIRRAHUM WA NAJWAAHUM WA ANNAL LAAHA A’LLAAMUL GHOYOOB.\nDo they not know that Allah knows their secret [thoughts] and [hears] their secret talks, and that Allah is knower of all that is Unseen?\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَلْمِزُوْنَ الْمُطَّوِّعِيْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ فِى الصَّدَقٰتِ وَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يَجِدُوْنَ اِلَّا جُهْدَهُمْ فَيَسْخَرُوْنَ مِنْهُمْؕ سَخِرَ اللّٰهُ مِنْهُمْ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(79)\nLAZEENA YALMEZOONAL MUTTAWWE-E’ENA MENAL MOAMENEENA FIS SADAQAATE WAL LAZEENA LAA YAJEDOONA ILLAA JOHDAHUM FA-YASKHAROONA MINHUM, SAKHERAL LAAHO MINHUM, WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nThose who blame the voluntary donors from among the faithful concerning the charities—and as for those who do not find [anything] except [what] their means [permit], they ridicule them—Allah shall put them to ridicule, and there is a painful punishment for them.\nاِسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ اَوْ لَا تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْؕ اِنْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ سَبْعِيْنَ مَرَّةً فَلَنْ يَّغْفِرَ اللّٰهُ لَهُمْؕ ذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(80)\nISTAGHFIR LAHUM AW LAA TASTAGHFIR LAHUM, IN TASTAGHFIR LAHUM SAB-E’ENA MARRATAN FALAN-Y YAGHFERAL LAAHO LAHUM, ZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM KAFAROO BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEH, WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAL FAASEQEEN.\nWhether you plead forgiveness for them or do not plead forgiveness for them, even if you plead forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah shall never forgive them because they defied Allah and His Apostle; and Allah does not guide the transgressing lot.\nفَرِحَ الْمُخَلَّفُوْنَ بِمَقْعَدِهِمْ خِلٰفَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ وَكَرِهُوْۤا اَنْ يُّجَاهِدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَقَالُوْا لَا تَنْفِرُوْا فِى الْحَرِّؕ قُلْ نَارُ جَهَنَّمَ اَشَدُّ حَرًّاؕ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(81)\nFAREHAL MOKHALLAFOONA BE-MAQ-A’DEHIM KHELAAFA RASOOLIL LAAHE WA KAREHOO AN-Y YOJAAHEDOO BE-AMWAALEHIM WA ANFOSEHIM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA QAALOO LAA TANFEROO FIL HAR, QUL NAARO JAHANNAMA ASHADDO HARRAA, LAW KAANOO YAFQAHOON.\nThose who were left behind boasted for sitting back against [the command of] the Apostle of Allah, and were reluctant to wage jihad with their possessions and persons in the way of Allah, and they said, ‘Do not go forth in this heat.’ Say, The fire of hell is severer in heat, should they understand.\nفَلْيَضْحَكُوْا قَلِيْلاً وَّلْيَبْكُوْا كَثِيْرًا ۚ جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(82)\nFALYAZHAKOO QALEELANW WAL YABKOO KASEERAA, JAZAAA-AM BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nSo let them laugh a little; much will they weep as a requital for what they used to earn.\nفَاِنْ رَّجَعَكَ اللّٰهُ اِلٰى طَآئِفَةٍ مِّنْهُمْ فَاسْتَاْذَنُوْكَ لِلْخُرُوْجِ فَقُلْ لَّنْ تَخْرُجُوْا مَعِىَ اَبَدًا وَّلَنْ تُقَاتِلُوْا مَعِىَ عَدُوًّا ؕ اِنَّكُمْ رَضِيْتُمْ بِالْقُعُوْدِ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ فَاقْعُدُوْا مَعَ الْخٰلِفِيْنَ‏(83)\nFA-IR RAJA-A’KAL LAAHO ELAA TAAA-EFATIM MINHUM FASTAAZANOOKA LIL-KHOROOJE FA-QUL LAN TAKHROJOO MA-E’YA ABADANW WA LAN TOQAATELOO MA-E’YA A’DUWWAA, INNAKUM RAZEETUM BIL-QO-O’ODE AWWALA MARRATIN FAQ-O’DOO MA-A’L KHAALEFEEN.\nIf Allah brings you back [from the battlefront] to a group of them and they seek your permission to go forth, say, ‘You shall never go forth with me, and you shall not fight with me against any enemy. You were indeed pleased to sit back the first time, so sit back with those who stay behind.’\nوَلَا تُصَلِّ عَلٰٓى اَحَدٍ مِّنْهُمْ مَّاتَ اَبَدًا وَّلَا تَقُمْ عَلٰى قَبْرِهٖ ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَمَاتُوْا وَهُمْ فٰسِقُوْنَ‏(84)\nWA LAA TOSALLE A’LAA AHADIM MINHUM MAATA ABADANW WA LAA TAQUM A’LAA QABREH, INNAHUM KAFAROO BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WA MAATOO WA HUM FAASEQOON.\nAnd never pray over any of them when he dies, nor stand at his graveside. They indeed defied Allah and His Apostle and died as transgressors.\nوَلَا تُعْجِبْكَ اَمْوَالُهُمْ وَاَوْلَادُهُمْؕ اِنَّمَا يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُّعَذِّبَهُمْ بِهَا فِى الدُّنْيَا وَتَزْهَقَ اَنْفُسُهُمْ وَهُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(85)\nWA LAA TO’JIBKA AMWAALOHUM WA AWLAADOHUM, INNAMAA YOREEDUL LAAHO AN-Y YO-A’ZZEBAHUM BEHAA FID DUNYAA WA TAZHAQA ANFOSOHUM WA HUM KAAFEROON.\nLet not their possessions or their children impress you. Allah only desires to punish them with these in this world, and that their souls may depart while they are faithless.\nوَاِذَاۤ اُنْزِلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ اَنْ اٰمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَجَاهِدُوْا مَعَ رَسُوْلِهِ اسْتَاْذَنَكَ اُولُوا الطَّوْلِ مِنْهُمْ وَقَالُوْا ذَرْنَا نَكُنْ مَّعَ الْقٰعِدِيْنَ‏(86)\nWA EZAA UNZELAT SOORATUN AN AAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WA JAAHEDOO MA-A’ RASOOLEHIS TAAZANAKA OOLUT TAWLE MINHUM WA QAALOO ZARNAA NAKUM MA-A’L QAA-E’DEEN.\nWhen a surah is sent down [declaring]: ‘Have faith in Allah, and wage jihad along with His Apostle, the affluent among them ask you for leave, and say, ‘Let us remain with those who sit back.’\nرَضُوْا بِاَنْ يَّكُوْنُوْا مَعَ الْخَوَالِفِ وَطُبِعَ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(87)\nRAZOO BE-AN-Y YAKOONOO MA-A’L KHAWAALEFE WA TOBE-A’ A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM FAHUM LAA YAFQAHOON.\nThey are pleased to be with those who stay back, and their hearts have been sealed. So they do not understand.\nلٰكِنِ الرَّسُوْلُ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ جَاهَدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْؕ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمُ الْخَيْرٰتُ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(88)\nLAAKENIR RASOOLO WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU JAAHADOO BE-AMWAALEHIM WA ANFOSEHIM, WA OOLAAA-EKA LAHOMUL KHAYRAAT, WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nBut the Apostle and the faithful who are with him wage jihad with their possessions and persons, and to such belong all the blessings, and it is they who are the felicitous.\nاَعَدَّ اللّٰهُ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(89)\nA-A’DDAL LAAHO LAHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, ZAALEKAL FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nAllah has prepared for them gardens with streams running in them, to remain in them [forever]. That is the great success.\nوَ جَآءَ الْمُعَذِّرُوْنَ مِنَ الْاَعْرَابِ لِيُؤْذَنَ لَهُمْ وَقَعَدَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَبُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ ؕ سَيُصِيْبُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(90)\nWA JAAA-AL MO-A’ZZEROONA MENAL A-A’RAABE LE-YOAZANA LAHUM WA QA-A’DAL LAZEENA KAZABUL LAAHA WA RASOOLAH, SAYOSEEBUL LAZEENA KAFAROO MINHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nSome of the Bedouins who sought to be excused came, so that they may be granted leave [to stay back]; while those who lied to Allah and His Apostle sat back. Soon there shall visit the faithless among them a painful punishment.\nلَيْسَ عَلَى الضُّعَفَآءِ وَلَا عَلَى الْمَرْضٰى وَلَا عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَجِدُوْنَ مَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ حَرَجٌ اِذَا نَصَحُوْا لِلّٰهِ وَ رَسُوْلِهٖؕ مَا عَلَى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ مِنْ سَبِيْلٍؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌۙ‏(91)\nLAYSA A’LAZ ZO-A’FAAA-E WA LAA A’LAL MARZAA WA LAA A’LAL LAZEENA LAA YAJEDOONA MAA YUNFEQOONA HARAJUN EZAA NASAHOO LILLAAHE WA RASOOLEH, MAA A’LAL MOHSENEENA MIN SABEEL, WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nThere is no blame on the weak, nor on the sick, nor on those who do not find anything to spend, so long as they are sincere to Allah and His Apostle. There is no [cause for] blaming the virtuous, and Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nوَّلَا عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اِذَا مَاۤ اَتَوْكَ لِتَحْمِلَهُمْ قُلْتَ لَاۤ اَجِدُ مَاۤ اَحْمِلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ تَوَلَّوْا وَّاَعْيُنُهُمْ تَفِيْضُ مِنَ الدَّمْعِ حَزَنًا اَلَّا يَجِدُوْا مَا يُنْفِقُوْنَؕ‏(92)\nWA LAA A’LAL LAZEENA EZAA MAA ATAWKA LE-TAHMELAHUM QULTA LAA AJEDO MAA AHMELOKUM A’LAYH, TAWALLAW WA A-A’YONOHUM TAFEEZO MENAD DAM-E’ HAZANAN ALLAA YAJEDOO MAA YUNFEQOON.\nNor [is there any blame] on those to whom, when they came to you to provide them with a mount, you said, ‘I do not find any mount for you,’ and they turned back, their eyes flowing with tears, grieved because they did not find any means to spend.\nاِنَّمَا السَّبِيْلُ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَاْذِنُوْنَكَ وَهُمْ اَغْنِيَآءُۚ رَضُوْا بِاَنْ يَّكُوْنُوْا مَعَ الْخَوَالِفِۙ وَطَبَعَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(93)\nINNAMAS SABEELO A’LAL LAZEENA YASTAAZENOONAKA WA HUM AGHNEYAAA, RAZOO BE-AN-Y YAKOONOO MA-A’L KHAWAALEFE, WA TABA-A’L LAAHO A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM FAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nThe blame lies only on those who ask leave of you [to stay behind] though they are well-off. They are pleased to be with those who stay back; Allah has set a seal on their hearts, so they do not know [the outcome of their conduct].\nيَعْتَذِرُوْنَ اِلَيْكُمْ اِذَا رَجَعْتُمْ اِلَيْهِمْ ؕ قُلْ لَّا تَعْتَذِرُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ لَكُمْ قَدْ نَبَّاَنَا اللّٰهُ مِنْ اَخْبَارِكُمْ ؕ وَ سَيَرَى اللّٰهُ عَمَلَكُمْ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ ثُمَّ تُرَدُّوْنَ اِلٰى عٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(94)\nYA’TAZEROONA ELAYKUM EZAA RAJA’TUM ELAYHIM, QUL LAA TA’TAZEROO LAN NOAMENA LAKUM QAD NABBA-ANAL LAAHO MIN AKHBAAREKUM, WA SAYARAL LAAHO A’MALAKUM WA RASOOLOHU SUMMA TORADDOONA ELAA A’ALEMIL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE FA-YONABBE-OKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nThey will offer you excuses when you return to them. Say, ‘Do not make excuses; we will never believe you. Allah has informed us of your state of affairs. Allah and His Apostle will observe your conduct, then you will be returned to the Knower of the sensible and the Unseen, and He will inform you concerning what you used to do.’\nسَيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ لَكُمْ اِذَا انْقَلَبْتُمْ اِلَيْهِمْ لِتُعْرِضُوْا عَنْهُمْؕ فَاَعْرِضُوْا عَنْهُمْؕ اِنَّهُمْ رِجْسٌ وَّمَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُۚ جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(95)\nSAYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE LAKUM EZAN QALABTUM ELAYHIM LE-TO’REZOO A’NHUM, FA-A-A’REZOO A’NHUM, INNAHUM RIJS, WA MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM, JAZAAA-AM BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nThey will swear to you by Allah when you return to them, that you may leave them alone. So leave them alone. They are indeed filth, and their refuge shall be hell, a requital for what they used to earn.\nيَحْلِفُوْنَ لَكُمْ لِتَرْضَوْا عَنْهُمْۚ فَاِنْ تَرْضَوْا عَنْهُمْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَرْضٰى عَنِ الْقَوْمِ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(96)\nYAHLEFOONA LAKUM LE-TARZAW A’NHUM, FA-IN TARZAW A’NHUM FA-INNAL LAAHA LAA YARZAA A’NIL QAWMIL FAASEQEEN.\nThey swear to you that you may be reconciled to them. But even if you are reconciled to them, Allah shall not be reconciled to the transgressing lot.\nاَلْاَعْرَابُ اَشَدُّ كُفْرًا وَّ نِفَاقًا وَّاَجْدَرُ اَلَّا يَعْلَمُوْا حُدُوْدَ مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِهٖؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(97)\nAL-A’RAABO ASHADDO KUFRANW WA NEFAAQANW WA AJDARO ALLAA YA’LAMOO HODOODA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO A’LAA RASOOLEH, WAL LAAHO A’LEEMUN HAKEEM.\nThe Bedouins are more obdurate in unfaith and hypocrisy, and more apt to be ignorant of the precepts that Allah has sent down to His Apostle, and Allah is all-knowing, all-wise.\nوَمِنَ الْاَعْرَابِ مَنْ يَّتَّخِذُ مَا يُنْفِقُ مَغْرَمًا وَّيَتَرَبَّصُ بِكُمُ الدَّوَآئِرَؕ عَلَيْهِمْ دَآئِرَةُ السَّوْءِؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(98)\nWA MENAL A-A’RAABE MAN-Y YATTAKHEZO MAA YUNFEQO MAGHRAMANW WA YATARABBASO BEKOMUD DAWAAA-ER, A’LAYHIM DAAA-ERATUS SAW, WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nAmong the Bedouins are those who regard what they spend as a loss, and they watch for a reversal of your fortunes. Theirs shall be an adverse turn of fortune, and Allah is all-hearing, all-knowing.\nوَمِنَ الْاَعْرَابِ مَنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَيَتَّخِذُ مَا يُنْفِقُ قُرُبٰتٍ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَصَلَوٰتِ الرَّسُوْلِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّهَا قُرْبَةٌ لَّهُمْؕ سَيُدْخِلُهُمُ اللّٰهُ فِىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(99)\nWA MENAL A-A’RAABE MAN-Y YOAMENO BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA YATTAKHEZO MAA YUNFEQO QOROBAATIN I’NDAL LAAHE WA SALAWAATIR RASOOL, ALAA INNAHAA QURBATUL LAHUM, SAYUDKHELOHOMUL LAAHO FEE RAHMATEH, INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nYet among the Bedouins are [also] those who believe in Allah and the Last Day, and regard what they spend as [a means of attaining] nearness to Allah and the blessings of the Apostle. Now, it shall indeed bring them nearness, and Allah will admit them into His mercy. Indeed Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nوَالسّٰبِقُوْنَ الْاَوَّلُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُهٰجِرِيْنَ وَالْاَنْصَارِ وَالَّذِيْنَ اتَّبَعُوْهُمْ بِاِحْسَانٍ ۙ رَّضِىَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوْا عَنْهُ وَاَعَدَّ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ تَحْتَهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(100)\nWAS SAABEQOONAL AWWALOONA MENAL MOHAAJEREENA WAL ANSAARE WAL LAZEENAT TABA-O’OHUM BE-EHSAANIR, RAZEYAL LAAHO A’NHUM WA RAZOO A’NHO WA A-A’DDA LAHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE TAHTAHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAA, ZAALEKAL FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nThe early vanguard of the Emigrants and the Helpers and those who followed them in virtue—Allah is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him, and He has prepared for them gardens with streams running in them, to remain in them forever. That is the great success.\nوَمِمَّنْ حَوْلَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَعْرَابِ مُنٰفِقُوْنَ ۛؕ وَمِنْ اَهْلِ الْمَدِيْنَةِ  ۛمَرَدُوْا عَلَى النِّفَاقِلَا تَعْلَمُهُمْ ؕ نَحْنُ نَعْلَمُهُمْ ؕ سَنُعَذِّبُهُمْ مَّرَّتَيْنِ ثُمَّ يُرَدُّوْنَ اِلٰى عَذَابٍ عَظِيْمٍ ۚ‏(101)\nWA MIMMAN HAWLAKUM MENAL A-A’RAABE MONAAFEQOON, WA MIN AHLIL MADEENAH, MARADOO A’LAN NEFAAQ, LAA TA’LAMOHUM, NAHNO NA’LAMOHUM, SANO-A’ZZEBOHUM MARRATAYNE SUMMA YORADDOONA ELAA A’ZAABIN A’ZEEM.\nThere are hypocrites among the Bedouins around you and among the townspeople of Madinah, steeped in hypocrisy. You do not know them; We know them, and We will punish them twice, then they shall be consigned to a great punishment.\nوَاٰخَرُوْنَ اعْتَرَفُوْا بِذُنُوْبِهِمْ خَلَطُوْا عَمَلًا صَالِحًا وَّاٰخَرَ سَيِّئًا ؕ عَسَى اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّتُوْبَ عَلَيْهِمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(102)\nWA AAKHAROONA’TARAFOO BE-ZONOOBEHIM KHALATOO A’MALAN SAALEHANW WA AAKHARA SAYYE-AA, A’SAL LAAHO AN-Y YATOOBA A’LAYHIM, INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\n[There are] others who have confessed to their sins, having mixed up righteous conduct with other that was evil. Maybe Allah will accept their repentance. Indeed Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nخُذْ مِنْ اَمْوَالِهِمْ صَدَقَةً تُطَهِّرُهُمْ وَتُزَكِّيْهِمْ بِهَا وَصَلِّ عَلَيْهِمْؕ اِنَّ صَلٰوتَكَ سَكَنٌ لَّهُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(103)\nKHUZ MIN AMWAALEHIM SADAQATAN TOTAHHEROHUM WA TOZAKKEEHIM BEHAA WA SALLE A’LAYHIM, INNA SALAATAKA SAKANUL LAHUM, WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nTake charity from their possessions to cleanse them and purify them thereby, and bless them. Indeed your blessing is a comfort to them, and Allah is all-hearing, all-knowing.\nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ يَقْبَلُ التَّوْبَةَ عَنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَيَاْخُذُ الصَّدَقٰتِ وَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(104)\nALAM YA’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA HOWA YAQBALUT TAWBATA A’N E’BAADEHI WA YAAKHOZUS SADAQAATE WA ANNAL LAAHA HOWAT TAWWAABUR RAHEEM.\nDo they not know that it is Allah who accepts the repentance of His servants and receives the charities, and that it is Allah who is the All-clement, the All-merciful?\nوَقُلِ اعْمَلُوْا فَسَيَرَى اللّٰهُ عَمَلَكُمْ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ وَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَؕ وَسَتُرَدُّوْنَ اِلٰى عٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَۚ‏(105)\nWA QOLE’MALOO FASAYARAL LAAHO A’MALAKUM WA RASOOLOHU WAL MOAMENOON, WA SATORADDOONA ELAA A’ALEMIL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE FA-YONABBE-OKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd say, ‘Go on working: Allah will see your conduct, and His Apostle and the faithful [as well], and you will be returned to the Knower of the sensible and the Unseen, and He will inform you concerning what you used to do.\nوَاٰخَرُوْنَ مُرْجَوْنَ لِاَمْرِ اللّٰهِ اِمَّا يُعَذِّبُهُمْ وَاِمَّا يَتُوْبُ عَلَيْهِمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(106)\nWA AAKHAROONA MURJAWNA LE-AMRIL LAAHE IMMAA YO-A’ZZEBOHUM WA IMMAA YATOOBO A’LAYHIM, WAL LAAHO A’LEEMUN HAKEEM.\n[There are] others waiting Allah’s edict: either He shall punish them, or turn to them clemently, and Allah is all-knowing, all-wise.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا مَسْجِدًا ضِرَارًا وَّكُفْرًا وَّتَفْرِيْقًۢا بَيْنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَاِرْصَادًا لِّمَنْ حَارَبَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ مِنْ قَبْلُؕ وَلَيَحْلِفُنَّ اِنْ اَرَدْنَاۤ اِلَّا الْحُسْنٰىؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَشْهَدُ اِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(107)\nWAL LAZEENAT TAKHAZOO MASJEDAN ZERAARANW WA KUFRANW WA TAFREEQAM BAYNAL MOAMENEENA WA IRSAADAL LEMAN HAARABAL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU MIN QABL, WA LAYAHLEFUNNA IN ARADNAA ILLAL HUSNAA, WAL LAAHO YASH-HADO INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nAs for those who took to a mosque for sabotage and for defiance, and to cause division among the faithful, and for the purpose of ambush [used] by those who have fought Allah and His Apostle before—they will surely swear, ‘We desired nothing but good,’ and Allah bears witness that they are indeed liars.\nلَا تَقُمْ فِيْهِ اَبَدًا ؕ لَمَسْجِدٌ اُسِّسَ عَلَى التَّقْوٰى مِنْ اَوَّلِ يَوْمٍ اَحَقُّ اَنْ تَقُوْمَ فِيْهِؕ فِيْهِ رِجَالٌ يُّحِبُّوْنَ اَنْ يَّتَطَهَّرُوْا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُطَّهِّرِيْنَ‏(108)\nLAA TAQUM FEEHE ABADAA, LA-MASJEDUN USSESA A’LAT TAQWAA MIN AWWALE YAWMIN AHAQQO AN TAQOOMA FEEH, FEEHE REJAALUN-Y YOHIBBOONA AN-Y YATATAHHAROO, WAL LAAHO YOHIBBUL MUTTAHHEREEN.\nDo not stand in it ever! A mosque founded on Godwariness from the [very] first day is worthier that you stand in it [for prayer]. Therein are men who love to keep pure, and Allah loves those who keep pure.\nاَفَمَنْ اَسَّسَ بُنْيَانَهٗ عَلٰى تَقْوٰى مِنَ اللّٰهِ وَرِضْوَانٍ خَيْرٌ اَمْ مَّنْ اَسَّسَ بُنْيَانَهٗ عَلٰى شَفَا جُرُفٍ هَارٍ فَانْهَارَ بِهٖ فِىْ نَارِ جَهَنَّمَؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(109)\nAFAMAN ASSASA BUNYAANAHU A’LAA TAQWAA MENAL LAAHE WA RIZWAANIN KHAYRUN AM MAN ASSASA BUNYAANAHU A’LAA SHAFAA JOROFIN HAARIN FANHAARA BEHI FEE NAARE JAHANNAM, WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nIs he who founds his building on Godwariness and [the pursuit of Allah’s] pleasure better-off or he who founds his building on the brink of a collapsing bank which collapses with him into the fire of hell? Allah does not guide the wrongdoing lot.\nلَا يَزَالُ بُنْيَانُهُمُ الَّذِىْ بَنَوْا رِيْبَةً فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَقَطَّعَ قُلُوْبُهُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(110)\nLAA YAZAALO BUNYAANOHOMUL LAZEE BANAW REEBATAN FEE QOLOOBEHIM ILLAA AN TAQATTA-A’ QOLOOBOHUM, WAL LAAHO A’LEEMUN HAKEEM.\nThe building they have built will never cease to be [a source of] disquiet in their hearts until their hearts are cut into pieces, and Allah is all-knowing, all-wise.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ اشْتَرٰى مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَاَمْوَالَهُمْ بِاَنَّ لَهُمُ الْجَنَّةَ ؕ يُقَاتِلُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَيَقْتُلُوْنَ وَ يُقْتَلُوْنَوَعْدًا عَلَيْهِ حَقًّا فِى التَّوْرٰٮةِ وَالْاِنْجِيْلِ وَالْقُرْاٰنِ ؕ وَمَنْ اَوْفٰى بِعَهْدِهٖ مِنَ اللّٰهِ فَاسْتَبْشِرُوْا بِبَيْعِكُمُ الَّذِىْ بَايَعْتُمْ بِهٖ ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(111)\nINNAL LAAHASH TARAA MENAL MOAMENEENA ANFOSAHUM WA AMWAALAHUM BE-ANNA LAHOMUL JANNAH, YOQAATELOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FA-YAQTOLOONA WA YUQTALOON, WA’DAN A’LAYHE HAQQAN FIT TAWRAATE WAL INJEELE WAL QUR-AAN, WA MAN AWFAA BE-A’HDEHI MENAL LAAHE FASTABSHEROO BE-BAY-E’KOMUL LAZEE BAAYA’TUM BEH, WA ZAALEKA HOWAL FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nIndeed Allah has bought from the faithful their souls and their possessions for paradise to be theirs: they fight in the way of Allah, kill, and are killed. A promise binding upon Him in the Torah and the Evangel and the Quran. And who is truer to his promise than Allah? So rejoice in the bargain you have made with Him, and that is the great success.\nاَلتَّاۤئِبُوْنَ الْعٰبِدُوْنَ الْحٰمِدُوْنَ السّاۤئِحُوْنَ الرّٰكِعُوْنَ السّٰجِدُوْنَ الْاٰمِرُوْنَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَالنَّاهُوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَالْحٰفِظُوْنَ لِحُدُوْدِ اللّٰه ِؕ وَبَشِّرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(112)\nTAAA-EBOONAL A’ABEDOONAL HAAMEDOONAS SAAA-EHOONAR RAAKE-O’ONAS SAAJEDOONAL AAMEROONA BIL-MA’ROOFE WAN NAAHOONA A’NIL MUNKARE WAL HAAFEZOONA LE-HODOODIL LAAH, WA BASH-SHERIL MOAMENEEN.\n[The faithful are] penitent, devout, celebrators of Allah’s praise, wayfarers, who bow [and] prostrate [in prayer], bid what is right and forbid what is wrong, and keep Allah’s bounds—and give good news to the faithful.\nمَا كَانَ لِلنَّبِىِّ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْاۤ اَنْ يَّسْتَغْفِرُوْا لِلْمُشْرِكِيْنَ وَ لَوْ كَانُوْۤا اُولِىْ قُرْبٰى مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمْ اَنَّهُمْ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(113)\nMAA KAANA LIN-NABIYYE WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AN-Y YASTAGHFEROO LIL-MUSHREKEENA WA LAW KAANOO OOLEE QURBAA MIM BA’DE MAA TABAYYANA LAHUM ANNAHUM ASHAABUL JAHEEM.\nThe Prophet and the faithful may not plead for the forgiveness of the polytheists, even if they should be [their] relatives, after it has become clear to them that they will be the inmates of hell.\nوَمَا كَانَ اسْتِغْفَارُ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ لِاَبِيْهِ اِلَّا عَنْ مَّوْعِدَةٍ وَّعَدَهَاۤ اِيَّاهُ ۚ فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهٗۤ اَنَّهٗ عَدُوٌّ لِّلّٰهِ تَبَرَّاَ مِنْهُ ؕ اِنَّ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ لَاَوَّاهٌ حَلِيْمٌ‏(114)\nWA MAA KAANAS TIGHFAARO IBRAAHEEMA LE-ABEEHE ILLAA A’M MAW-E’DATINW WA-A’DAHAA IYYAAH, FALAMMAA TABAYYANA LAHU ANNAHU A’DUWWUL LILLAAHE TABARRA-A MINH, INNA IBRAAHEEMA LA-AWWAAHUN HALEEM.\nAbraham’s pleading forgiveness for his father was only to fulfill a promise he had made him. So when it became manifest to him that he was an enemy of God, he repudiated him. Indeed Abraham was most plaintive and forbearing.\nوَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيُضِلَّ قَوْمًۢا بَعْدَ اِذْ هَدٰٮهُمْ حَتّٰى يُبَيِّنَ لَهُمْ مَّا يَتَّقُوْنَؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(115)\nWA MAA KAANAL LAAHO LE-YOZILLA QAWMAM BA’DA IZ HADAAHUM HATTAA YOBAYYENA LAHUM MAA YATTAQOON, INNAL LAAHA BE-KULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nAllah does not lead any people astray after He has guided them until He has made clear to them what they should beware of. Indeed Allah has knowledge of all things.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُؕ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(116)\nINNAL LAAHA LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, YOHYEE WA YOMEET, WA MAA LAKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MINW WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nIndeed to Allah belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the earth. He gives life and brings death. And besides Allah you do not have any guardian or helper.\nلَقَدْ تَّابَ اللّٰهُ عَلَى النَّبِىِّ وَالْمُهٰجِرِيْنَ وَالْاَنْصَارِ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّبَعُوْهُ فِىْ سَاعَةِ الْعُسْرَةِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا كَادَ يَزِيْغُ قُلُوْبُ فَرِيْقٍ مِّنْهُمْ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْؕ اِنَّهٗ بِهِمْ رَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌۙ ‏(117)\nLAQAT TAABAL LAAHO A’LAN NABIYYE WAL MOHAAJEREENA WAL ANSAARIL LAZEENAT TABA-O’OHO FEE SAA-A’TIL U’SRATE MIM BA’DE MAA KAADA YAZEEGHO QOLOOBO FAREEQIM MINHUM SUMMA TAABA A’LAYHIM, INNAHU BEHIM RA-OOFUR RAHEEM.\nCertainly Allah turned clemently to the Prophet and the Emigrants and the Helpers, who followed him in the hour of difficulty, after the hearts of a part of them were about to swerve. Then He turned clemently to them—indeed, He is most kind and merciful to them\nوَّعَلَى الثَّلٰثَةِ الَّذِيْنَ خُلِّفُوْا ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا ضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْاَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ اَنْفُسُهُمْ وَظَنُّوْۤا اَنْ لَّا مَلْجَاَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ اِلَّاۤ اِلَيْهِ ؕ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ لِيَتُوْبُوْا  ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(118)\nWA A’LAS SALAASATIL LAZEENA KHULLEFOO, HATTAA EZAA ZAAQAT A’LAYHEMUL ARZO BEMAA RAHOBAT WA ZAAQAT A’LAYHIM ANFOSOHUM WA ZANNOO AL LAA MALJA-A MENAL LAAHE ILLAA ELAYH, SUMMA TAABA A’LAYHIM LE-YATOOBOO, INNAL LAAHA HOWAT TAWWAABUR RAHEEM.\n—and to the three who were left behind. When the earth became narrow for them with [all] its expanse, and their own souls weighed heavily on them, and they knew that there was no refuge from Allah except in Him, then He turned clemently toward them so that they might be penitent. Indeed Allah is the All-clement, the All-merciful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَكُوْنُوْا مَعَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(119)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUT TAQUL LAAHA WA KOONOO MA-A’S SAADEQEEN.\nO you who have faith! Be wary of Allah, and be with the Truthful.\nمَا كَانَ لِاَهْلِ الْمَدِيْنَةِ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهُمْ مِّنَ الْاَعْرَابِ اَنْ يَّتَخَلَّفُوْا عَنْ رَّسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ وَ لَا يَرْغَبُوْا بِاَنْفُسِهِمْ عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ لَا يُصِيْبُهُمْ ظَمَاٌ وَّلَا نَصَبٌ وَّلَا مَخْمَصَةٌ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا يَطَئُوْنَ مَوْطِئًا يَّغِيْظُ الْكُفَّارَ وَلَا يَنَالُوْنَ مِنْ عَدُوٍّ نَّيْلاً اِلَّا كُتِبَ لَهُمْ بِهٖ عَمَلٌ صَالِحٌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَۙ‏(120)\nMAA KAANA LE-AHLIL MADEENATE WA MAN HAWLAHUM MENAL A-A’RAABE AN-Y YATAKHALLAFOO A’R RASOOLIL LAAHE WA LAA YARGHABOO BE-ANFOSEHIM A’N NAFSEH, ZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM LAA YOSEEBOHUM ZAMA-UNW WA LAA NASABUNW WA LAA MAKHMASATUN FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA LAA YATA-OONA MAWTE-AN-Y YAGHEEZUL KUFFAARA WA LAA YANAALOONA MIN A’DUWWIN NAYLAN ILLAA KOTEBA LAHUM BEHI A’MALUN SAALEH, INNAL LAAHA LAA YOZEE-O’ AJRAL MOHSENEEN.\nIt is not fitting for the people of Madinah and the Bedouins around them to hang back behind the Apostle of Allah and prefer their own lives to his life. That is because they neither experience any thirst, nor fatigue, nor hunger, in the way of Allah, nor do they tread any ground enraging the faithless, nor do they gain any ground against an enemy but a righteous deed is written for them on its account. Indeed Allah does not waste the reward of the virtuous.\nوَلَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ نَفَقَةً صَغِيْرَةً وَّلَا كَبِيْرَةً وَّلَا يَقْطَعُوْنَ وَادِيًا اِلَّا كُتِبَ لَهُمْ لِيَجْزِيَهُمُ اللّٰهُ اَحْسَنَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(121)\nWA LAA YUNFEQOONA NAFAQATAN SAGHEERATANW WA LAA KABEERATANW WA LAA YAQTA-O’ONA WAADEYAN ILLAA KOTEBA LAHUM LE-YAJZEYAHOMUL LAAHO AHSANA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nAnd neither do they incur any expense, big or small, nor do they cross any valley, but it is written to their account, so that Allah may reward them by the best of what they used to do.\nوَمَا كَانَ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ لِيَنْفِرُوْا كَآفَّةً ؕ فَلَوْلَا نَفَرَ مِنْ كُلِّ فِرْقَةٍ مِّنْهُمْ طَآئِفَةٌ لِّيَتَفَقَّهُوْا فِى الدِّيْنِ وَ لِيُنْذِرُوْا قَوْمَهُمْ اِذَا رَجَعُوْۤا اِلَيْهِمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَحْذَرُوْنَ‏(122)\nWA MAA KAANAL MOAMENOONA LE-YANFEROO KAAFFAH, FALAWLAA NAFARA MIN KULLE FIRQATIM MINHUM TAAA-EFATUL LE-YATAFAQQAHOO FID DEENE WA LE-YUNZEROO QAWMAHUM EZAA RAJA-O’O ELAYHIM LA-A’LLAHUM YAHZAROON.\nYet it is not for the faithful to go forth en masse. But why should not there a group from each of their sections go forth to become learned in religion, and to warn their people when they return to them, so that they may beware?\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا قَاتِلُوا الَّذِيْنَ يَلُوْنَكُمْ مِّنَ الْكُفَّارِ وَلْيَجِدُوْا فِيْكُمْ غِلْظَةً  ؕ وَاعْلَمُوْاۤ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(123)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO QAATELUL LAZEENA YALOONAKUM MENAL KUFFAARE WAL YAJEDOO FEEKUM GHILZAH, WA’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nO you who have faith! Fight the faithless who are in your vicinity, and let them find severity in you, and know that Allah is with the Godwary.\nوَاِذَا مَاۤ اُنْزِلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ فَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّقُوْلُ اَيُّكُمْ زَادَتْهُ هٰذِهٖۤ اِيْمَانًا ۚ فَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا فَزَادَتْهُمْ اِيْمَانًا وَّهُمْ يَسْتَبْشِرُوْنَ‏(124)\nWA EZAA MAA UNZELAT SOORATUN FAMINHUM MAN-Y YAQOOLO AYYOKUM ZAADATHO HAAZEHI EEMAANAA, FA-AMMAL LAZEENA AAMANOO FA-ZAADATHUM EEMAANANW WA HUM YASTABSHEROON.\nWhenever a surah is sent down, there are some of them who say, ‘Which of you did it increase in faith?’ As for those who have faith, it increases them in faith, and they rejoice.\nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ فَزَادَتْهُمْ رِجْسًا اِلٰى رِجْسِهِمْ وَمَاتُوْا وَهُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(125)\nWA AMMAL LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN FA-ZAADATHUM RIJSAN ELAA RIJSEHIM WA MAATOO WA HUM KAAFEROON.\nBut as for those in whose heart is a sickness, it only adds defilement to their defilement, and they die while they are faithless.\nاَوَلَا يَرَوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ يُفْتَنُوْنَ فِىْ كُلِّ عَامٍ مَّرَّةً اَوْ مَرَّتَيْنِ ثُمَّ لَا يَتُوْبُوْنَ وَلَا هُمْ يَذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(126)\nAWA LAA YARAWNA ANNAHUM YUFTANOONA FEE KULLE A’AMIM MARRATAN AW MARRATAYNE SUMMA LAA YATOOBOONA WA LAA HUM YAZZAKKAROON.\nDo they not see that they are tried once or twice every year? Yet they neither repent, nor do they take admonition.\nوَاِذَا مَاۤ اُنْزِلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ نَّظَرَ بَعْضُهُمْ اِلٰى بَعْضٍؕ هَلْ يَرٰٮكُمْ مِّنْ اَحَدٍ ثُمَّ انْصَرَفُوْا ؕ صَرَفَ اللّٰهُ قُلُوْبَهُمْ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(127)\nWA EZAA MAA UNZELAT SOORATUN NAZARA BA’ZOHUM ELAA BA’Z, HAL YARAAKUM MIN AHADIN SUMMAN SARAFOO, SARAFAL LAAHO QOLOOBAHUM BE-ANNAHUM QAWMUL LAA YAFQAHOON.\nWhenever a surah is sent down they look at one another: ‘Is anybody observing you?’ Then they slip away. Allah has turned aside their hearts, for they are a people who do not understand.\nلَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْ اَنْفُسِكُمْ عَزِيْزٌ عَلَيْهِ مَا عَنِتُّمْ حَرِيْصٌ عَلَيْكُمْ بِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ رَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(128)\nLAQAD JAAA-AKUM RASOOLUM MIN ANFOSEKUM A’ZEEZUN A’LAYHE MAA A’NITTUM HAREESUN A’LAYKUM BIL-MOAMENEENA RA-OOFUR RAHEEM.\nThere has certainly come to you an apostle from among yourselves. Grievous to him is your distress; he has deep concern for you, and is most kind and merciful to the faithful.\nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَقُلْ حَسْبِىَ اللّٰهُ ۖ  لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ؕ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ ؕ وَهُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(129)\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FA-QUL HASBEYAL LAAH, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO, A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTO WA HOWA RABBUL A’RSHIL A’ZEEM. (129)\nBut if they turn their backs [on you], say, ‘Allah is sufficient for me. There is no god except Him. In Him I have put my trust and He is the Lord of the Great Throne.’",
  "merits": "This Surah has 129 verses and was revealed in Madinah. This Surah was revealed all at once and its revelation was accompanied by seventy thousand angels. It is narrated that keeping this Surah over one’s head (like in a cap or Amama) is a safety from thieves and destruction of property by fire. Also, keeping this Surah in one’s possession ensures safety from the evil designs of enemies."
